//! `stashed` returns a thunk that captures a region-bound input.
//!
//! The returned thunk would outlive its caller. The checker refuses it as
//! `KeptEscaped`.
//!
//! The source places `k` in a thunk with no region. Rust refuses
//! `fn stash<'a>(k: &'a T) -> &'static T`.
//!
//! - see: corpus/model/regions/lent.gandr — a thunk at the caller region

/// `stash` returns a thunk that forces its region-bound input.
@[ refuses("KeptEscaped") ]
def stash[r : Region](k : (() -> Integer) at r) -> () -> Integer =
  pure thunk { force k }
